   "reason": "Both the drop and the detonation are free actions, so a knight materialises inside the guard cluster and explodes in the same turn — every enemy on its eight knight-squares dies (plus the ring at T3+), the king is stunned 2-3 turns, and Rookie has not moved yet. | Enemies rate an ally queen as highly as Rookie, so a Duchess normally dies in a turn; while Rookie is smoked the king cannot flee her threats and the summon's captures do NOT break the smoke (only Rookie's own do), so the queen can carve while Rookie stays invisible.",
